 demand for health insurance coverage by low-income workers: Can reduced premiums achieve full coverage?</article-title><source>Health Services Research</source><year>1997</year><volume>32</volume><fpage>453</fpage><lpage>471</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9327813</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B18"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Zhang</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Wang</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Wang</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Hsiao</surname><given-names>W</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Social capital and farmers' willingness to join a newly established community-based health insurance in rural China</article-title><source>Health Policy</source><year>2006</year><volume>76</volume><fpage>233</fpage><lpage>242</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16046027</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/j.healthpol.2005.06.001</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B19"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Dib</surname><given-names>HH</given-names></name><name><surname>Pan</surname><given-names>X</given-names></name><name><surname>Zhang</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Evaluation of the new rural cooperative medical system in China: Is it working or not?</article-title><source>International Journal for Equity in Health</source><year>2008</year><volume>7</volume><fpage>17</fpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">18590574</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1186/1475-9276-7-17</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B20"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Wang</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Yip</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Zhang</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Wang</surname><given-names>L</gi